      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "Confirm the correct starting point, then guide the learner to apply conservation of momentum.",
      "content": "Exactly. There is no external horizontal force, so total momentum stays zero. What should the two trolleys' momenta add up to after they move apart?"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I think p_X + p_Y = 0, but I don't know what that means for the options."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "The learner has the conservation equation but needs to distinguish momentum direction from magnitude. From p_X + p_Y = 0, p_X = -p_Y, so their directions are opposite and their magnitudes are equal. Illustrative tool check only: if p_Y = +1 unit, then p_X = 0 - 1 = -1 unit, whose magnitude is 1. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"0 - 1\") -> -1]",
