      "content": "Yes: the parallel component is 40 cos 25° ≈ 36.25 N. For Q, the weight component down the incline is 3 × 9.8 × sin 30° = 14.7 N, so:\n\n40 cos 25° − T − 14.7 = 3a\n\nAdd this to P’s equation, T − 9.8 − 2.5 = 2a. The tensions cancel:\n\n36.25 − 14.7 − 9.8 − 2.5 = 5a\n9.25 = 5a, so a ≈ 1.85 m·s⁻².\n\nThe magnitude of P’s acceleration is $1{,}85\\text{ m}\\cdot\\text{s}^{-2}$."
